WEBVTT

00:02.253 --> 00:04.548
<i>♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.633 --> 00:07.680
<i>♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.766 --> 00:11.272
<i>♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.357 --> 00:14.029
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.114 --> 00:17.619
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:17.748 --> 00:21.296
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.381 --> 00:22.841
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:22.926 --> 00:25.221
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:25.266 --> 00:30.066
<i>♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:33.827 --> 00:35.036
Good news, peter.

00:35.121 --> 00:36.916
We finally saved enough money

00:36.960 --> 00:38.962
To go on a couple's
vacation together.

00:39.048 --> 00:40.925
We haven't traveled in years.

00:41.052 --> 00:43.264
That's not true.
You made us drive to toronto

00:43.350 --> 00:45.728
To confront that sex worker
I facetime with.

00:45.814 --> 00:48.150
Yeah, that wasn't a vacation,
that was an ultimatum.

00:48.277 --> 00:52.244
And after an insultingly
long pause, I chose you.

00:52.371 --> 00:54.707
We're going on a trip, peter.

00:55.712 --> 00:56.838
Aw, sweet.

00:56.965 --> 00:59.970
<i> Harold goldfarb:
Jetpack lawyer is on.</i>

01:00.055 --> 01:02.434
<i> Your honor,
may I approach the bench?</i>

01:02.562 --> 01:04.438
Is this so you can use
your jet pack?

01:04.567 --> 01:05.733
Yes.

01:05.902 --> 01:06.986
I'll allow it.

01:07.072 --> 01:09.618
<i> (l.A. Law theme playing)</i>

01:09.745 --> 01:13.501
(shouting): I'm appealing this
to a higher court.

01:13.628 --> 01:14.881
I wish I had a jet pack.

01:14.966 --> 01:16.634
My life would be better.

01:16.720 --> 01:18.054
(electronic chirping)

01:18.182 --> 01:20.225
Ooh, 360.

01:21.440 --> 01:23.609
Oh, wait. 180.
Very good.

01:23.694 --> 01:24.987
Now let's get your height.

01:25.114 --> 01:27.911
All right.
So you're seven foot, six, 180,

01:28.039 --> 01:29.707
With colorectal cancer.

01:29.792 --> 01:31.461
I'm tall?

01:34.261 --> 01:37.350
Excuse me, I'm here
to renew my passport.

01:37.393 --> 01:40.733
Of course, let's go take
a terrible photo.

01:40.860 --> 01:43.739
Oh, my god, that's why
she wore the nice shirt.

01:43.824 --> 01:47.122
Oh, this is so sad.

01:49.046 --> 01:52.051
(gasps) oh, no!
Seal and heidi klum broke up.

01:52.178 --> 01:54.515
Uh, yeah, in 2012.

01:54.642 --> 01:57.020
All those magazines
are super old.

01:57.106 --> 01:58.358
(gasps) good lord.

01:58.485 --> 02:00.947
Whitney houston died?
Since when?

02:00.991 --> 02:03.077
Again, 2012.

02:03.121 --> 02:05.165
This says she drowned
in the bathtub.

02:05.293 --> 02:07.379
But-but I take baths.

02:07.464 --> 02:09.759
I think there may have been
other stuff going on.

02:09.845 --> 02:11.681
No! Baths kill, chris.

02:11.766 --> 02:14.228
And I will not become
another statistic.

02:14.314 --> 02:16.567
Next time I bathe,
I'm taking a shower.

02:16.652 --> 02:19.115
And it's gonna be
the best baby shower ever.

02:19.200 --> 02:20.827
I'll wear a tiara, go to brunch,

02:20.996 --> 02:22.497
And my best friend
will start crying,

02:22.624 --> 02:24.837
And that's when we realize
she's been trying for years.

02:25.006 --> 02:26.674
And I'll say,
"it's not your fault,"

02:26.760 --> 02:29.221
But quietly I wonder if it's
a result of her life choices.

02:29.349 --> 02:31.393
I mean, I'm as liberal as
anyone, but do you really think

02:31.521 --> 02:33.982
A throuple based on
a mutual love of cocaine

02:34.069 --> 02:35.235
Doesn't have consequences?

02:35.363 --> 02:37.825
I am as liberal
as anyone, though.

02:43.716 --> 02:45.218
Are you sure
you want to do this, peter?

02:45.345 --> 02:46.679
Seems a little reckless.

02:46.723 --> 02:48.434
You do know that
wearing a jet pack doesn't

02:48.520 --> 02:51.023
-Make you a lawyer, right?
-Objection.

02:51.150 --> 02:52.485
Not supporting my dream
of becoming

02:52.612 --> 02:54.614
-A sky attorney.
-Withdrawn.

02:54.700 --> 02:56.954
Hey, I saw a thing
and now I want to do the thing.

02:57.039 --> 02:58.666
That's my thing.

02:58.751 --> 03:01.506
Now, quit yapping and tape
these leaf blowers to my back.

03:01.592 --> 03:04.471
<i> (l.A. Law theme playing)</i>

03:08.275 --> 03:10.485
To a thousand and beyond.

03:10.571 --> 03:13.409
That's as high as he can count.

03:17.170 --> 03:18.296
(laughs)

03:18.381 --> 03:19.967
-(falcons screeching)
-(exclaims)

03:20.052 --> 03:21.679
(shouts)

03:22.766 --> 03:24.768
(screaming)

03:27.152 --> 03:28.862
Peter, what the hell?

03:28.947 --> 03:31.034
Aah! Aah!

03:31.161 --> 03:33.415
(crashing, glass shattering)

03:35.296 --> 03:38.175
Aw, crap, there's one of them
chinese balloons.

03:38.260 --> 03:40.556
Excuse me. I'm japanese.

03:40.642 --> 03:42.185
Oh, my god. I am so sorry.

03:42.270 --> 03:43.480
Please excuse my ignorance.

03:43.607 --> 03:46.654
Hey, just take this opportunity
to learn and grow.

03:46.782 --> 03:50.704
I will.
I will, balloon, I will.

03:53.881 --> 03:56.510
Man, lois was pissed
about me wrecking the house.

03:56.679 --> 03:59.685
Really? I assumed she'd be numb
to your shenanigans by now.

03:59.812 --> 04:01.856
Worst part is I spent
all our vacation money

04:02.025 --> 04:03.527
On the jet pack without asking.

04:03.612 --> 04:05.407
For some reason,
women don't like it

04:05.534 --> 04:07.494
When you wreck
their financial future.

04:07.580 --> 04:10.210
The lady brain
is truly the most confounding

04:10.254 --> 04:11.671
Of all head meats.

04:11.715 --> 04:13.884
Peter, I know what it's like
to be in the doghouse,

04:13.970 --> 04:15.346
But I think I can help.

04:15.432 --> 04:17.602
Why don't you use
my mom's condo in florida?

04:17.688 --> 04:19.440
Every year she winters
in buffalo.

04:19.567 --> 04:21.777
I keep telling her
she's doing florida wrong,

04:21.864 --> 04:23.324
But she doesn't listen.

04:23.409 --> 04:25.161
Thanks, joe.
Florida sounds great.

04:25.289 --> 04:26.497
I bet lois'll love that.

04:26.625 --> 04:28.669
My mom winters in a coffin.

04:29.466 --> 04:31.509
All the seasons, really.

04:35.688 --> 04:37.523
Brian, I need your help
to take a shower.

04:37.692 --> 04:40.822
Shower?! No way.
Dogs and showers don't mix.

04:40.949 --> 04:43.537
Come on, bri, you're the only
one who can do this with me.

04:43.707 --> 04:46.544
I can't go back there.
I'm sorry, it's just...

04:46.630 --> 04:49.636
I took a shower once.
I was so young.

04:49.763 --> 04:51.848
(flute playing)

04:51.892 --> 04:53.477
<i> When they put me in the tub,</i>

04:53.562 --> 04:55.148
<i> I figured it was just
to rub my tummy.</i>

04:55.234 --> 04:57.112
<i> What a fool I was.</i>

04:58.659 --> 05:00.578
<i> They stripped me down
like an animal.</i>

05:00.664 --> 05:03.000
<i>And that's when things got real.</i>

05:08.390 --> 05:09.808
<i> The water just kept coming.</i>

05:10.018 --> 05:12.313
<i>I tried to fight back, but I was
half-blind from the soap.</i>

05:12.399 --> 05:14.862
<i> At first, peter tried
to bathe me from the side,</i>

05:14.947 --> 05:17.659
<i> But then he realized
it'd be easier if he...</i>

05:17.786 --> 05:18.955
<i> Got in.</i>

05:20.878 --> 05:22.087
<i> When it was over,</i>

05:22.298 --> 05:24.676
<i> They just wiped me down
with an old beach towel</i>

05:24.803 --> 05:26.931
<i> And threw me in the yard.</i>

05:29.648 --> 05:30.857
<i> I didn't get a parade.</i>

05:30.942 --> 05:32.988
<i> Hell, I didn't even get
a chew toy.</i>

05:33.073 --> 05:35.075
Thank you for your shower.

05:36.163 --> 05:37.498
Don't do this, stewie.

05:37.583 --> 05:39.377
Once you get in that shower,
you never come back.

05:39.463 --> 05:41.173
Sorry, but I'm taking
a shower...

05:41.301 --> 05:43.136
"with or without you."

05:43.263 --> 05:45.099
Uh, we-we can't afford
that u2 song.

05:45.185 --> 05:46.394
Oh, really?

05:46.563 --> 05:49.150
But they will pay us
to play one off their new album.

05:49.277 --> 05:51.657
Yeah, that's a big bon-no.

06:01.097 --> 06:04.019
Well, peter, I was skeptical,
but I got to say,

06:04.146 --> 06:05.480
It's beautiful here.

06:05.608 --> 06:07.150
Well, this is the address.

06:22.982 --> 06:25.235
Peter, this isn't
a vacation home,

06:25.321 --> 06:27.282
This is a retirement community.

06:27.367 --> 06:28.953
I can't believe
you never told me.

06:29.039 --> 06:31.166
Lois, we had
a whole conversation about this

06:31.293 --> 06:33.880
When you were passed out
on your airplane pills.

06:34.635 --> 06:36.011
Okay, I got to fess up,

06:36.096 --> 06:38.183
It's kind of
a retirement community.

06:38.226 --> 06:41.524
If you're okay with it,
breathe once every minute.

06:43.530 --> 06:46.076
-(snores)
-ah, there it is.

06:55.225 --> 06:58.480
I can't believe you took me
to a retirement community.

06:58.565 --> 06:59.650
Come on, it's not so bad.

06:59.777 --> 07:01.738
There's canasta and pickleball,

07:01.865 --> 07:04.577
Plus the world's softest
toilet seats.

07:06.794 --> 07:09.214
I can't poop now
'cause I'm afraid of heights.

07:09.341 --> 07:11.636
-(air hissing)
-uhp, here we go.

07:11.764 --> 07:14.268
All right,
now I'm getting confidence.

07:22.998 --> 07:25.920
Ugh, there's so much
"not actual milk" milk.

07:26.006 --> 07:27.966
Hey, I think this is
that mother's day gift

07:28.052 --> 07:29.136
Joe told me about.

07:29.221 --> 07:30.346
It's a "joe-mometer."

07:30.474 --> 07:33.480
It announces celebrity trivia
in joe's voice.

07:33.607 --> 07:35.400
<i> Joe:
It's 76 degrees.</i>

07:35.569 --> 07:37.907
<i> Actor morgan freeman
is left-handed.</i>

07:37.992 --> 07:40.204
Wow.
That's mildly interesting.

07:40.289 --> 07:42.876
This place is depressing.
I want to go home.

07:42.961 --> 07:45.633
Oh, hey, I know this isn't
the trip you were hoping for,

07:45.718 --> 07:46.969
But our flight back
isn't for a week,

07:47.097 --> 07:48.890
So we may as well
try to have fun.

07:48.975 --> 07:51.271
Ugh, fine.
I'll give it a shot.

07:51.357 --> 07:52.733
You won't be disappointed.

07:52.819 --> 07:54.362
Remember, you didn't think
you'd like it

07:54.447 --> 07:56.575
When I had big,
giant traps either.

07:57.539 --> 07:59.374
Hey, babe,
did you wash my singlet?

07:59.459 --> 08:01.294
I got a tournament
up in great neck.

08:01.454 --> 08:02.882
Peter, I can't wash your singlet

08:03.009 --> 08:04.845
And make you
a hundred egg whites.

08:04.972 --> 08:07.183
-Hey, dad. (exclaims)
-(grunting)

08:07.269 --> 08:09.063
Uhp, left yourself open
to a nearside cradle.

08:09.149 --> 08:11.862
-I am not a part of this.
-Well, then tap out.

08:11.947 --> 08:14.242
-I tap out. (choking)
-no tap outs.

08:14.327 --> 08:16.164
(mellow music playing)

08:21.094 --> 08:22.094
(gasps)

08:22.221 --> 08:24.140
(sexy music playing)

08:33.246 --> 08:36.544
Good god, these are the ones
who could make it to the pool.

08:36.630 --> 08:39.050
Imagine what the ones
in the rooms look like.

08:39.135 --> 08:40.721
I, uh, couldn't help but notice

08:40.848 --> 08:43.393
Your sternum
has only 14 sunspots.

08:43.479 --> 08:46.735
Uh, no one here
has less than 83.

08:46.905 --> 08:48.865
Aw, I bet you say that
to all the ladies

08:48.951 --> 08:50.953
Who can walk without assistance.

08:51.039 --> 08:52.123
You ever been with a man

08:52.251 --> 08:55.004
Who knows
the price of milk in 1942?

08:55.090 --> 08:57.009
(weak chuckle)
can't say that I have.

08:57.095 --> 08:58.136
It was a nickel.

08:58.222 --> 08:59.849
That was the price
of everything then.

08:59.977 --> 09:01.853
A suit was a nickel.
A house was a nickel.

09:01.982 --> 09:03.692
A dime was a nickel.

09:04.863 --> 09:07.284
Hemorrhoid donut for the lady?

09:09.916 --> 09:12.045
A girl could get used to this.

09:12.131 --> 09:15.135
Now, who wants to see me bite
into an apple with my own teeth?

09:15.296 --> 09:16.513
It's suicide!

09:16.598 --> 09:19.437
I missed the moon landing,
I ain't missing this.

09:20.775 --> 09:24.282
-(cheering)
-heavens to betsy,
that's amazing.

09:28.753 --> 09:30.922
Could you help us
turn on the tv, dear?

09:31.008 --> 09:33.386
Our favorite program
is about to start.

09:33.472 --> 09:34.890
Sure, why not.

09:34.975 --> 09:37.021
<i> -(l.A. Law theme playing)
-ooh!
-Ooh!</i>

09:37.148 --> 09:40.069
You must be one of those
computer whizzes.

09:40.154 --> 09:42.951
The last time I tried
to work the remote myself,

09:43.079 --> 09:45.331
I got folded inside a bed.

09:45.459 --> 09:49.884
Could you reach that
cigar box full of dominoes?

09:49.969 --> 09:51.554
My grandchildren are coming

09:51.640 --> 09:54.686
And I want them
to do something fun.

09:54.815 --> 09:57.777
Oh, such a strong boy.

09:57.905 --> 10:00.116
Here, have a chick-o-stick.

10:00.243 --> 10:02.288
You carry candy in your pocket?

10:02.416 --> 10:03.666
Of course.

10:03.752 --> 10:07.551
All old ladies
are 70% pocket candy.

10:07.636 --> 10:09.179
Werther's.

10:09.306 --> 10:10.933
Butterscotch.

10:11.018 --> 10:13.522
That weird strawberry candy
with the goo inside.

10:13.608 --> 10:15.903
You guys are like
walking piñatas.

10:16.866 --> 10:18.742
(giggling)

10:18.829 --> 10:22.461
Oh, it's so nice to be touched.

10:27.224 --> 10:29.435
All right,
before the big shower,

10:29.562 --> 10:30.563
I should do a dry run.

10:30.648 --> 10:32.860
Need to get a feel
for the space.

10:33.990 --> 10:36.117
Let's start with
some articulation exercises.

10:36.203 --> 10:38.039
Soap the shins.
Soap the shins.

10:38.208 --> 10:40.336
Soap and sop
and soak the shins.

10:40.421 --> 10:42.841
The room sound is a little
tinny, but I can make it work.

10:43.010 --> 10:44.846
All right,
not bad for the first day.

10:45.016 --> 10:46.643
Rupert, toss over
the rope ladder.

10:46.770 --> 10:47.811
Rupert?

10:47.939 --> 10:50.902
Oh, you son of a bitch,
I knew it.

10:50.987 --> 10:52.490
Is this because
I suggested a prenup?

10:52.617 --> 10:55.579
Well, if money doesn't matter,
you should just sign it.

10:59.341 --> 11:00.591
(grunts)

11:02.765 --> 11:03.766
I'm stuck!

11:03.851 --> 11:05.353
Help!

11:08.821 --> 11:10.741
(panting)

11:10.827 --> 11:12.202
Oh, this is just great.

11:12.288 --> 11:15.459
I'm going to die in here
and I'll never take a shower.

11:15.545 --> 11:18.467
Maybe you won't, but we will.

11:18.553 --> 11:19.469
Really?

11:19.555 --> 11:21.307
Thanks, bri.

11:22.311 --> 11:24.941
The poop was in there
when I got in.

11:28.827 --> 11:31.331
Man, this place is great
for my self-esteem.

11:31.416 --> 11:33.336
I'm getting bicep squeezes
left and right.

11:33.463 --> 11:36.468
And men keep telling me
I look like greer garson.

11:36.554 --> 11:37.971
That's good, I think.

11:38.098 --> 11:39.725
Being the youngest,
healthiest people here

11:39.852 --> 11:41.062
Sure has its perks.

11:41.147 --> 11:44.111
It's like everyone
wants a piece of us.

11:48.624 --> 11:51.837
Before we harvest the organs
of these two young meatbags,

11:51.923 --> 11:54.093
We need to decide who gets what.

11:54.179 --> 11:57.266
So, if you want a body part,
call dibs now.

11:57.394 --> 12:00.483
Yeah, I'll take
the udders and the hooves.

12:00.610 --> 12:02.613
What? That's not a cow.

12:02.699 --> 12:04.325
That's a guy?

12:04.411 --> 12:06.371
But I saw him
eating grass earlier.

12:06.415 --> 12:09.002
Yeah, yeah, yeah, we're
donating the brain to science.

12:09.130 --> 12:10.548
No one take the brain.

12:19.905 --> 12:20.990
Morning, peter.

12:21.075 --> 12:23.119
I brought you some
calcium-rich milk.

12:23.204 --> 12:26.335
It'll make your bones strong
so I can swim again.

12:26.421 --> 12:28.549
-Thanks, art.
-Don't thank me--

12:28.676 --> 12:30.344
The cow did most of the work.

12:30.430 --> 12:32.141
(both laughing)

12:34.189 --> 12:36.734
Lois, would you be a dear

12:36.820 --> 12:38.490
And lift this fruitcake

12:38.617 --> 12:40.911
That's the same weight
as my grandson?

12:41.039 --> 12:42.624
Um, sure?

12:43.878 --> 12:47.009
Full range of motion.
Firm grip.

12:47.136 --> 12:49.640
Time for your breakfast
eye exam.

12:49.767 --> 12:51.186
Which line can you read?

12:51.313 --> 12:53.232
Uh, well, I can read "gledjeb".

12:53.359 --> 12:56.782
That's not a word, it's just
random letters in a row.

12:56.952 --> 12:58.745
Really?
I thought it was dutch.

12:58.831 --> 13:00.290
Hey!
They said my name.

13:00.376 --> 13:02.286
Don't be so self-centered.

13:02.380 --> 13:05.427
They could mean
gledjeb opeldark.

13:09.731 --> 13:11.233
Well, you ready, stewie?

13:11.318 --> 13:13.947
Yup. Even got some decals
for the shower floor.

13:13.991 --> 13:15.785
I see you went with
the flower design.

13:15.871 --> 13:17.038
The daffodil pattern provides

13:17.124 --> 13:18.658
Superior protection
against slippage.

13:18.711 --> 13:21.339
Dr. Scholl's gave it
four toes out of seven.

13:21.425 --> 13:23.929
I-it's a weird scale,
but that's still pretty good.

13:24.056 --> 13:25.600
And I got us some shampoo.

13:25.727 --> 13:28.148
Why did you buy the kind
for color-treated hair?

13:28.275 --> 13:31.070
<i>Speaking of hair, that is one
heck of a musical, huh?</i>

13:31.157 --> 13:33.117
That's the hair
we should be discussing.

13:33.202 --> 13:35.373
You got a little
giuliani drip going there.

13:36.628 --> 13:39.466
There were voting
irregularities in michigan!

13:43.686 --> 13:46.816
Can you believe they gave us
complimentary massages?

13:47.821 --> 13:49.113
Welcome!

13:49.199 --> 13:51.452
Have you fasted
for the last 12 hours?

13:51.579 --> 13:53.708
-Were we supposed to?
-No worries.

13:53.835 --> 13:56.255
Why do you need our blood
pressure for a massage?

13:56.341 --> 13:58.761
Deep tissue. Hot stone.

13:58.846 --> 14:00.432
We have all different kinds.

14:00.559 --> 14:01.810
You just ignored my question

14:01.937 --> 14:03.815
And answered a different one
you had in your head.

14:03.900 --> 14:06.863
I did eat my twin in the womb,
thanks for asking.

14:06.991 --> 14:09.745
Okay, let's get you started.

14:11.994 --> 14:14.674
Are you a d cup
or is that just gravity?

14:14.759 --> 14:16.386
Oh, just gravity.

14:16.471 --> 14:18.266
Just a half rack, tony.

14:19.395 --> 14:23.193
Excuse me,
I have to use the restroom.

14:28.207 --> 14:29.876
Oh, my god.

14:29.961 --> 14:32.340
(playing "tie a yellow ribbon
round the ole oak tree")

14:36.310 --> 14:38.856
Ah.
Well, that's not so bad.

14:41.237 --> 14:42.906
Hard to misinterpret that.

14:50.301 --> 14:53.389
(gasps) oh, my god!

14:54.937 --> 14:57.900
And how many drinks would
you say you consume each week?

14:57.985 --> 14:59.738
Socially, about four to six.

14:59.907 --> 15:02.995
Alone in the dark while crying
to adele, a hundred.

15:03.124 --> 15:05.501
Welp, beggars can't be choosers.

15:09.973 --> 15:10.889
(grunts)

15:11.058 --> 15:13.145
They're trying to
steal our organs.

15:13.188 --> 15:15.441
They want to kill us.
Let's go.

15:16.697 --> 15:18.365
-What's happening?
-Don't worry, lois.

15:18.492 --> 15:19.785
It's called "flintstone legs."

15:19.829 --> 15:21.874
Trust me, all we need
is some traction.

15:23.337 --> 15:24.797
Calling all coots!

15:24.883 --> 15:28.347
Red dawn and the waddler
have flown the coop.

15:33.486 --> 15:36.658
Brian, if something should
happen to one or both of us,

15:36.744 --> 15:39.456
I'd regret not having said this,
so I'm just gonna say it.

15:39.499 --> 15:41.461
You have a nice penis.

15:41.547 --> 15:43.799
I see it a lot,
I don't say anything,

15:43.885 --> 15:45.303
But it's nice.

15:45.347 --> 15:48.519
Now, you say something nice
about my penis.

15:48.605 --> 15:50.942
I think we should
turn the water on.

15:55.997 --> 15:58.334
(grunts)

16:00.591 --> 16:03.011
Huh, this isn't as bad
as I remember.

16:03.097 --> 16:04.139
It's actually kind of nice.

16:04.225 --> 16:06.395
I wonder what this thing does.

16:07.650 --> 16:09.025
(rattling)

16:09.112 --> 16:11.407
-Aah!
-Aah!

16:11.492 --> 16:13.578
-This is horrible!
-The spray is too strong.

16:13.622 --> 16:15.792
We have to turn down the water.

16:20.179 --> 16:22.558
Now it's too hot!
Now it's too cold!

16:22.643 --> 16:25.899
My god, how does chris
stay in here for 45 minutes?

16:26.027 --> 16:28.322
He's doing other stuff,
but we got to get out of here.

16:28.407 --> 16:31.663
Oh, my god,
now the tub is filling up.

16:31.790 --> 16:34.084
Wait a minute,
the tub is filling up.

16:34.212 --> 16:36.215
This isn't a shower anymore.

16:36.301 --> 16:38.804
This is a bath!
I know baths.

16:38.890 --> 16:40.308
I've got this, bri.

16:41.270 --> 16:43.983
("the wreck of
the edmund fitzgerald" playing)

16:45.822 --> 16:48.745
<i>♪ the legend lives on
from the chippewa on down ♪</i>

16:48.789 --> 16:50.874
<i>♪ of the big lake they called ♪</i>

16:50.960 --> 16:52.837
<i>♪ gitche gumee ♪</i>

16:55.137 --> 16:58.518
<i>♪ the lake, it is said,
never gives up her dead ♪</i>

16:58.603 --> 17:00.647
<i>♪ when the skies of November ♪</i>

17:00.690 --> 17:03.362
<i>♪ turn gloomy. ♪</i>

17:05.452 --> 17:07.414
Oh, my god.
What is that?

17:07.541 --> 17:10.379
A decade's worth of meg's hair.

17:10.506 --> 17:11.673
Ew, that's gross.

17:11.843 --> 17:15.474
No, it isn't.
It's our lifeline, brian.

17:18.232 --> 17:20.403
Boost me to the shower caddy.

17:21.157 --> 17:23.117
-Oh!
-(grunts)

17:26.377 --> 17:28.087
Hang on.

17:29.384 --> 17:31.011
(grunting)

17:35.063 --> 17:36.900
Aah! (grunts)

17:37.904 --> 17:40.825
We are never
taking a shower again.

17:40.911 --> 17:42.120
Agreed.

17:42.247 --> 17:45.712
Uh, fellas, I'm gonna need
the room for 45 minutes.

18:00.457 --> 18:02.167
(grunts)

18:02.253 --> 18:03.671
-(tires screeching)
-(grunts)

18:03.798 --> 18:06.386
I'm gonna gut you like a fish

18:06.513 --> 18:09.350
And scoop out your insides.

18:09.435 --> 18:11.856
Right after I parallel park.

18:13.112 --> 18:14.445
Peter, come on!

18:14.615 --> 18:15.865
Sorry, lois.
As a man,

18:15.993 --> 18:18.707
I'm required to watch
other men parallel park.

18:18.834 --> 18:21.588
Peter, he wants to kill us!
Let's go!

18:26.602 --> 18:27.643
You got to cut the wheel.

18:27.729 --> 18:30.358
I am cutting the wheel.

18:31.655 --> 18:35.161
-No, the other way.
-This is the other way, jerk.

18:36.584 --> 18:37.709
No, left. Cut left.

18:37.836 --> 18:41.008
Pull back, cut left.
Now I'm involved.

18:41.093 --> 18:42.804
Right.

18:42.890 --> 18:44.809
Oh!
They shrunk the spaces

18:44.936 --> 18:47.942
So they could make more money.
(weak chuckle)

18:48.070 --> 18:50.531
Sir, this is a standard space
on a public street.

18:50.659 --> 18:52.577
Nobody's making money here.

18:58.718 --> 19:00.555
Stop where you are.

19:00.641 --> 19:04.815
We would like this all
to be over by 4:00 p.M., please.

19:07.156 --> 19:09.785
(growling)

19:11.374 --> 19:12.457
Enough!

19:12.543 --> 19:14.462
You freaks are never
getting our organs!

19:14.548 --> 19:17.302
Now shuffle aside
before I call the cops.

19:17.388 --> 19:18.722
This is florida, doll.

19:18.891 --> 19:21.438
The cops are all just strippers
who carry guns.

19:21.565 --> 19:23.275
-Then who are the strippers?
-Firemen.

19:23.360 --> 19:25.447
-So, who fights the fires?
-No idea.

19:25.575 --> 19:29.164
-You're sick.
-And you-- you're selfish.

19:29.207 --> 19:32.505
You come in here flaunting
your working ears and knuckles

19:32.674 --> 19:33.883
That don't look like an abacus

19:33.969 --> 19:36.723
And expect us
not to pick you clean

19:36.808 --> 19:39.271
Like the last hour
at a chinese buffet?

19:39.356 --> 19:44.993
If we have to take your organs
by force, then so be it.

19:45.078 --> 19:47.164
-Have it your way.
-(knuckles crack)

19:47.292 --> 19:48.709
We always do,

19:48.795 --> 19:51.592
No matter how many times
we have to send the entrée back.

19:51.677 --> 19:53.846
We will stand here
and fight until--

19:54.016 --> 19:56.645
-Woman: It's 4:04.
-Oh! We're missing dinner!

19:56.773 --> 19:58.984
(indistinct chatter)

20:00.698 --> 20:01.949
I'm sorry, lois.

20:02.076 --> 20:04.121
Looks like I ruined
another vacation.

20:04.207 --> 20:06.627
You know, peter, I was upset
when you brought me here

20:06.754 --> 20:09.174
Because I wanted to have
an exciting vacation,

20:09.261 --> 20:10.511
Just the two of us,

20:10.596 --> 20:12.641
And I thought this place
was gonna be boring,

20:12.768 --> 20:14.645
But you know what?
Turns out

20:14.730 --> 20:16.818
Fleeing from bloodthirsty
senior citizens with you

20:16.903 --> 20:18.697
Was kind of a thrill.

20:18.824 --> 20:20.910
This may not have been
the vacation I expected

20:21.037 --> 20:24.085
But it turned out to be
the best one I've ever had.

20:24.170 --> 20:25.588
I love you, peter.

20:25.673 --> 20:27.216
I love you, too.

20:29.433 --> 20:30.851
Man, this place is crazy.

20:30.936 --> 20:33.565
Can you believe joe
was in the dark about all this?

20:33.609 --> 20:35.653
Did you get the legs?

20:35.781 --> 20:38.952
Damn it!
(inhales, exhales)

20:39.038 --> 20:40.456
No, no, no, it's fine.

20:40.584 --> 20:43.171
I'll see if I can get cleveland
to go down there next week.

20:53.698 --> 20:56.202
Hey, bud! How was florida?

20:56.245 --> 20:58.247
(playing "tie a yellow ribbon
round the ole oak tree")